{"name":"Apollo Bay","hex":"#748697","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Apollo Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A locality in Kingborough council area, south eastern Tasmania, Australia.","A town in the Shire of Colac Otway, south western Victoria, Australia"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Apollo_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apollo Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Apollo Bay is a coastal town in southwestern Victoria, Australia. It is situated on the eastern side of Cape Otway, along the edge of the Barham River and on the Great Ocean Road, in the Colac Otway Shire. The town had a population of 1,790 at the 2021 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Apollo_Bay_from_Mariners_Lookout.jpg/330px-Apollo_Bay_from_Mariners_Lookout.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo_Bay","wikidata":"Q619097"},{"title":"Apollo","blocks":[{"text":"Apollo is one of the Olympian deities in ancient Greek religion and mythology. His numerous functions include light, healing, prophecy, music, poetry, and archery. He is the son of Zeus and Leto, and the twin brother of Artemis, goddess of the hunt. He is considered to be the most beautiful god and is represented as the ideal of the kouros or ephebe, a beardless, athletic youth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Italy-3104_-_Apollo_%285378415112%29.jpg/330px-Italy-3104_-_Apollo_%285378415112%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apollo","wikidata":"Q37340"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay","wikidata":"Q39594"},{"title":"Bay (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Bay is a hair coat color of horses, characterized by a reddish-brown or brown body color with a black point coloration on the mane, tail, ear edges, and lower legs. Bay is one of the most common coat colors in many horse breeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/BayMare.jpg/330px-BayMare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay_(horse)","wikidata":"Q900906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Amphitrite_Australiastamp.jpg/500px-Amphitrite_Australiastamp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Amphitrite_Australiastamp.jpg/500px-Amphitrite_Australiastamp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1936 Stamp - Cable to Tasmania depicting the Greek goddess Amphitrite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmphitrite_Australiastamp.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Coastine_golf_australia.jpg/500px-Coastine_golf_australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Coastine_golf_australia.jpg/500px-Coastine_golf_australia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_camp